# Trivy exceptions.
#
# Plain format on purpose. The richer .trivyignore.yaml supports a
# machine-enforced `expired_at`, but it depends on both the action's
# `trivyignores` plumbing and a Trivy build new enough to parse YAML ignore
# files — and it silently did not apply in CI while working locally. A gate that
# behaves differently on a developer machine than on the runner is worse than a
# simpler one that behaves the same everywhere.
#
# The expiry is still ENFORCED, just by the other scanner: scripts/audit-gate.mjs
# carries the same advisory with `reviewBy: 2026-10-31` and fails the build once
# that date passes. It runs in this same job, immediately before Trivy. Both
# files must be updated together.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router, RSC-mode CSRF bypass.
#
# Not reachable. WatchTower is a client-only SPA using createBrowserRouter +
# RouterProvider, with no server rendering, no server actions, and no RSC APIs
# anywhere in Frontend/src (verified by grepping for unstable_*,
# matchRSCServerRequest and createStaticHandler).
#
# The fix is react-router 8.x, which requires Node >= 22.22.0 and would drop the
# Node 20 support that both the CI matrix and the runtime base image target —
# a larger regression than the risk being carried. Deferred to the Node 22
# baseline migration. Review by 2026-10-31.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
